## Verification & Measurement Methodology

### 1. Frequency Verification
The script uses SPICE `.meas` (measure) statements in the `.control` block to compute time differences between consecutive rising edges across a threshold voltage ($V_{th} = \\frac{V_{DD}}{2} = 0.6\\text{ V}$):
$$F_{div2} = \\frac{1}{T_{div2}}, \\quad F_{div4} = \\frac{1}{T_{div4}}$$

### 2. Duty Cycle Verification
Duty cycle is calculated by measuring pulse high-width ($T_{high}$) against the total period ($T_{period}$):
$$\\text{Duty Cycle (\\%)} = \\left(\\frac{T_{high}}{T_{period}}\\right) \\times 100$$
A toggle flip-flop feedback topology naturally forces a 50% duty cycle at the output.

### 3. Stage Chaining ($2^k$)
To form a divide-by-$N$ divider ($N = 2^k$):
- Stage 1 output (`div2_out`) acts as the clock input for Stage 2 (`div4_out`).
- Additional stages can be chained sequentially in the same manner.

